\code{feature37.speed}), \code{time_string} (same as \code{time_stamp_originTZ}), and
\code{time_bin} and \code{altitude_bin} (refer to radar database tables that are not
part of the package).
The package-level metadata (title, description, owner, licence, embargo,
contributors with ORCID and DataCite roles, related identifiers, suggested
citation) are read from \code{metadata}. Spatial and temporal coverage, the
applied filters and the provenance (database, birdscanR and classifier
versions) are added automatically.

When \code{outputDirPath} is provided, the package is written to
\verb{outputDirPath/<campaignID>/} as \code{datapackage.json} plus one compressed CSV
file per resource, ready for a Zenodo deposit.
